{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"init_"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This function must be called before using any other GTK functions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in your GUI applications."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It will initialize everything needed to operate the toolkit. In particular,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it will open the default display (see [func"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gdk.Display.get_default"},{"type":"text","text":"])."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you are using [class"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk\/Application"},{"type":"text","text":"], you usually don’t have to call this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"function; the [vfunc"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gio.Application.startup"},{"type":"text","text":"] handler does it for you. Though,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"if you are using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GApplication"},{"type":"text","text":" methods that will be invoked before "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"startup"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"local_command_line"},{"type":"text","text":", you may need to initialize GTK explicitly."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This function will terminate your program if it was unable to initialize"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the windowing system for some reason. If you want your program to fall back"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to a textual interface, call [func"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gtk.init_check"},{"type":"text","text":"] instead."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"GTK calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"signal (SIGPIPE, SIG_IGN)"},{"type":"text","text":" during initialization, to ignore"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SIGPIPE signals, since these are almost never wanted in graphical"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applications. If you do need to handle SIGPIPE for some reason, reset"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the handler after "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gtk_init()"},{"type":"text","text":", but notice that other libraries (e.g."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"libdbus or gvfs) might do similar things."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gtk\/init_()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk\/init_()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Initializes GTK."}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"init_"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"title":"init_()","roleHeading":"Function","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"func","externalID":"s:3Gtk5init_yyF","modules":[{"name":"Gtk"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk"]]},"references":{"doc://Gtk/documentation/Gtk":{"role":"collection","title":"Gtk","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gtk"},"doc://Gtk/documentation/Gtk/init_()":{"role":"symbol","title":"init_()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"init_"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Initializes GTK."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk\/init_()","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gtk\/init_()"},"doc://Gtk/documentation/Gtk/Application":{"role":"symbol","title":"Application","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Application"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A high-level API for writing applications."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gtk\/documentation\/Gtk\/Application","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Application"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gtk\/application"}}}